Z||000000||ct||11-09-2001||08:15 PM||||Your opinions on Lucas Oil  <A HREF="http://www.lucasoil.com/" TARGET=_blank>http://www.lucasoil.com/</A>  products, please.<P>Should I use them in my '85 Fiero GT?<P>Thanks.||||reg||1
Z||000001||Old Lar||11-09-2001||08:55 PM||||Their T shirts and crew jackets would look good in your Fiero.  Most oil additives are snake oil products which do little to improve a cars performance.  They will lighten your wallet.<P>A frequent oil change with a good quality oil (I've used 5-30 as recommended in my 87 GT since new)is a good way to keep the engine in good shape.  Maybe some injector cleaner in the gas, but thats about it.  Now this is assuming that your engine is in good shape to begine with.  If you have a well worn high milage engine, nothing other than a rebuild will get it back to its original performance.||||reg||1
